increment is near zero (e.g., Luyssaert et al., 2008). Peatlands are unlikely to saturate in carbon storage, but the rate of C uptake may be very slow (see Box 11.1).
Human and natural impacts. Soil and vegetation carbon sinks can be impacted upon by direct human-induced, indirect human-induced, and natural changes (Smith, 2005). All of the mitigation practices discussed in Section 11.3.1 arise from direct human-induced impacts (deliberate


